./makefile

	This file functions as a task runner.

./docs

	This directory contains documentation.

./docs/project.info

	This file documents what every file and
	directory in this repository is for. It
	is an input to the tree command,
	although it may be viewed by itself.

./docs/README.md

	You should read this before anything
	else. GitHub renders this file on the
	repository home page. It may also be
	read as is in a pager like less.

./docs/images

	This directory contains
	markdown-embedded images.

./docs/images/lain.png

	This file was obtained from the image
	sharing website imgur.com, and I do not
	claim any rights to it. I use it as the
	leading image in the readme file to
	entice the reader.
	Source: https://imgur.com/eeHqyyp

./docs/inventory/packages

	Each file in this directory is named
	after a package manager and contains
	line-delimited identifiers recognized by
	that package manager.

./docs/tutorials

	This directory contains technical
	tutorials written in markdown for my own
	future reference.

./packs

	This directory contains units of
	configuration packaged per software.

./packs/system-wide

	This directory contains system-wide
	configuration packages which should be
	deployed relative to the root directory.

./packs/user-specific

	This directory contains user-specific
	configuration packages which should be
	deployed relative to the user's $HOME
	directory.

./utils

	This directory contains
	post-installation utility scripts.

./utils/cold

	These are used occasionally.

./utils/hot

	These are used routinely and available
	on path for quick access.
